WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:26.089 --> 00:00:28.892
Or would you pretend you weren't alone?

00:00:36.099 --> 00:00:38.335
So, you wake up one day and find that

00:00:38.335 --> 00:00:40.904
you're the only person left in the world.

00:00:40.904 --> 00:00:42.205
Kind of cool, right?

00:00:42.205 --> 00:00:43.540
No obligations,

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:44.741
no rules,

00:00:44.741 --> 00:00:46.076
no limits. 

00:00:51.715 --> 00:00:54.251
Go for the exotic fruits first.

00:00:54.251 --> 00:00:57.287
If your mangos and bananas
are imported from overseas,

00:00:57.287 --> 00:00:59.489
chances are they'll be hard to come by.

00:00:59.489 --> 00:01:01.191
So eat them while you can,

00:01:01.191 --> 00:01:03.727
and enjoy every last bite.

00:01:08.999 --> 00:01:10.934
You might think that with no one stopping you,

00:01:10.934 --> 00:01:12.436
you could go anywhere.

00:01:12.436 --> 00:01:13.937
But not so fast!

00:01:13.937 --> 00:01:17.741
All those abandoned cars, boats,
and planes you see lying around

00:01:17.741 --> 00:01:21.411
will be useless in about 2 years
when their fuel goes stale.

00:01:21.411 --> 00:01:22.913
Guess you'll be sticking around.

00:01:22.913 --> 00:01:24.114
But for how long?

00:01:29.152 --> 00:01:30.020
If water,

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:30.554
food

00:01:30.554 --> 00:01:31.288
and shelter

00:01:31.288 --> 00:01:32.556
are your basic needs, 

00:01:32.556 --> 00:01:34.558
shelter would be the easiest to come by.

00:01:34.558 --> 00:01:37.694
You'd literally have a world
of homes to choose from!

00:01:37.694 --> 00:01:39.996
But be careful where you settle down.

00:01:39.996 --> 00:01:41.565
Cities would become dangerous,

00:01:41.565 --> 00:01:42.966
since without proper maintenance,

00:01:42.966 --> 00:01:45.402
they'd start to fall apart pretty quickly.

00:01:45.402 --> 00:01:47.571
Nature's elements: rain, frost, and heat,

00:01:47.571 --> 00:01:49.606
would take their toll.

00:01:49.606 --> 00:01:52.109
Rot and mold would become widespread,

00:01:52.109 --> 00:01:55.946
and vegetation would crack through
concrete and break through glass.

00:01:55.946 --> 00:02:00.417
But even if you were to fight back
against nature's reclamation of the land,

00:02:00.417 --> 00:02:03.920
all it takes is one bolt of lightning
to start a city-wide fire.

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:05.589
And you can't call the fire department.

00:02:05.589 --> 00:02:07.524
So run for the hills!

00:02:12.496 --> 00:02:14.865
But even the country isn't all that safe.

00:02:14.865 --> 00:02:18.235
First of all, there are predators
you'd need to defend against.

00:02:18.235 --> 00:02:20.804
Wild dogs, feral cats...

00:02:20.804 --> 00:02:22.472
bears...

00:02:22.472 --> 00:02:25.442
But you'd only have to worry about them
as long as you could still breathe.

00:02:25.442 --> 00:02:28.845
There are more than
400 nuclear power plants in the world.

00:02:28.845 --> 00:02:33.350
And once their automated safety systems
began to fail without human supervision,

00:02:33.350 --> 00:02:34.484
there would be meltdowns

00:02:34.484 --> 00:02:35.485
across the planet,

00:02:35.485 --> 00:02:38.255
rendering many regions
simply uninhabitable.

00:02:43.226 --> 00:02:44.261
In terms of food, 

00:02:44.261 --> 00:02:46.296
the city would be your best bet.

00:02:46.296 --> 00:02:50.233
Supermarkets have enough canned and
frozen food to last you for decades!

00:02:50.233 --> 00:02:51.535
Whereas in the country,

00:02:51.535 --> 00:02:53.837
crops and livestock would start to dwindle

00:02:53.837 --> 00:02:55.005
without proper care or

00:02:55.005 --> 00:02:56.907
protection from predators.

00:02:56.907 --> 00:02:58.942
But if natural is more your style,

00:02:58.942 --> 00:03:02.045
you'd have to go back to the old ways
of hunting with a spear or a bow,

00:03:02.045 --> 00:03:05.282
since ammunition would be
limited and harder to come by.

00:03:05.282 --> 00:03:07.484
Maybe you could grow your
own little vegetable garden,

00:03:07.484 --> 00:03:09.953
but that would cut into your water resources.

00:03:14.925 --> 00:03:17.594
Without other humans,
you'd be without electricity.

00:03:17.594 --> 00:03:20.664
Water pumping stations and
treatment works would shut down,

00:03:20.664 --> 00:03:24.467
and the fresh water kept in reservoirs
would go stale quite quickly.

00:03:24.467 --> 00:03:25.936
You could rely on bottled water,

00:03:25.936 --> 00:03:28.838
and you'd probably have
thousands of litres to go through,

00:03:28.838 --> 00:03:31.841
but eventually, you'd have to
learn how to purify your own.

00:03:36.813 --> 00:03:38.982
You'd have to teach yourself a lot of things,

00:03:38.982 --> 00:03:41.484
but lucky for you, you've got
a lot of time on your hands,

00:03:41.484 --> 00:03:44.588
and millions of books out there with
all the information you'd need

00:03:44.588 --> 00:03:46.723
to survive effectively on your own. 

00:03:46.723 --> 00:03:48.858
So, while it might be hard at first, 

00:03:48.858 --> 00:03:52.395
you could technically survive
as the last human on Earth.

00:03:52.395 --> 00:03:54.130
But would you really want to?

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:57.767
Humans evolved together as
social creatures in order to survive.

00:03:57.767 --> 00:04:00.203
We joined forces against
hunger and harsh weather;

00:04:00.203 --> 00:04:04.207
and built families and communities
to share stories, empathize,

00:04:04.207 --> 00:04:06.810
and keep each other happy and healthy.

00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:11.881
Human contact has been scientifically
proven to build trust and reduce stress.

00:04:11.881 --> 00:04:16.486
So, while it's apt to cramp your style,
be glad it's a small world,

00:04:16.486 --> 00:04:21.458
we need each other more than you think.

